---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Case Studies | Pikes Peak Web Designs"
description: "Case studies of sites I've built, written in plain words, with scores you can check yourself in free public tools."
permalink: /case-studies/
---

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span>Case studies</span>
    </nav>
    <span class="section-label">Case studies</span>
    <h1>Sites I've built, <em>with numbers you can check</em></h1>
    <p>Each case study covers a live site I built and the scores anyone can test. There are no paid-client case studies yet. Until the first client gives written permission, these are my own projects and a volunteer site for a hockey club.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:1080px">

    <div class="case-study-grid">
      {% for cs in caseStudies %}
        <a href="/case-studies/{{ cs.slug }}/" class="case-study-card{% if cs.selfStudy %} case-study-card--self{% endif %}{% if cs.screenshot %} case-study-card--shot{% endif %}">
          {% if cs.screenshot %}
          <div class="case-study-card-shot">
            {% image cs.screenshot, cs.client + " home page screenshot", "(min-width: 1100px) 480px, (min-width: 720px) 45vw, 92vw", [480, 760, 1100] %}
          </div>
          {% endif %}
          <div class="case-study-card-body">
            <div class="case-study-card-eyebrow">
              {% if cs.selfStudy and not cs.screenshot %}<span class="case-study-card-pill">My own business site</span>{% endif %}
              {% if cs.selfStudy and cs.screenshot %}<span class="case-study-card-pill">My own project</span>{% endif %}
              <span>{{ cs.trade }}{% if cs.metro %} &middot; {{ cs.metro }}{% endif %}</span>
            </div>
            <h2 class="case-study-card-title">{{ cs.client }}</h2>
            <p class="case-study-card-summary">{{ cs.summary }}</p>
            <div class="case-study-card-metrics">
              {% for m in cs.metrics %}
                {% if loop.index <= 3 %}
                <div class="case-study-card-metric">
                  <span class="case-study-card-metric-label">{{ m.label }}</span>
                  <strong class="case-study-card-metric-value">{{ m.value or m.after }}</strong>
                </div>
                {% endif %}
              {% endfor %}
            </div>
            <span class="case-study-card-cta">Read the case study &rarr;</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <aside class="case-study-fallback">
      <span class="section-label">More to come</span>
      <p>Client studies follow the publishing clause in the <a href="/agreement/" class="inline-link">service agreement</a>. Until the first one arrives, here's more you can check yourself:</p>
      <ul style="margin:1.25rem 0 0;line-height:1.9">
        <li><a href="/samples/" class="inline-link">Six demo sites</a> for six trades, each with its own look and every page custom-coded. Test any of them in <a href="https://pagespeed.web.dev" rel="noopener" class="inline-link">Google's speed test</a>.</li>
        <li><a href="/technical-approach/" class="inline-link">Technical approach</a>: the tools, the targets, and the measurements every site is held to.</li>
        <li><a href="/owners-guide/" class="inline-link">Owner's guide</a>: what every client receives on launch day, in plain language.</li>
      </ul>
    </aside>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta-section">
  <div class="cta-inner">
    <span class="section-label">Want your site to be the next case study?</span>
    <h2>Your site could be the next one here</h2>
    <p>Sign up when you're ready. If we're a good fit and you give written permission, I'll write up your site here too.</p>
    <div class="cta-buttons">
      <a href="/subscribe/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Start now</a>
    </div>
    <p class="cta-sub">Prefer to talk first? <a href="/contact/">Book a free call</a>. It takes 20 to 30 minutes on Google Meet.</p>
  </div>
</section>
